    <p><b>Strategy.</b> Circle equations: (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r² — center signs flip inside the parentheses, and the right side is r², never r. Sectors: reduce the angle fraction first, then multiply by πr². Learn the special families: 30–60–90 (x, x√3, 2x), 45–45–90 (x, x, x√2), and the 3-4-5 clan (6-8-10, 5-12-13, 7-24-25) — recognition beats computation. For shadows and mirrors, similar triangles give a single constant ratio; set it up once and multiply.</p>
